      <workList xml:id="workDesc_c17c9f26">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e223220">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_31270519">A4:008</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_25a18e3f" xml:lang="it">Sonata in A♯ per il cembalo</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_1e974da0">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_eff00898">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_b65ae81a">
               <p xml:id="idm115">A solo sonata in three movements for harpsichord. The two transcripts of the sonata, which both are located in Sweden, contain only minor differences. There is no indication of date of production but the script suggests that the copies were made sometime during the second half of the eighteenth century, presumably by professional copyists or perhaps experienced musical amateurs. A letter in the archives of Lund's University reveals that Friedrich Kraus, who was director and founder of the music society at the university (Lunds Akademiska kapellet) was in Stockholm in November 1754 transcribing music at the court's music archives. The collection, which includes the Scheibe sonata, is mentioned specifically. Thus the manuscript now in Uppsala was used for Kraus' transcription. The use of G2-clef in the upper stave suggests a production closer to the mid-eighteenth century rather than the late eighteenth century. The sonata is not identical to any of those that appear in the Breitkopf catalogues with incipits.</p>
            </history>
